from h34 import *
M=mcq;F=tf;S=short;N=num
chapter(3,'evs','staying-healthy-and-happy','Staying Healthy and Happy',
 ('Moyna and her Dadu\'s neem twig','Moyna\'s grandfather Dadu cleans his teeth with a fresh twig of neem or babool, not a toothbrush. Moyna tries a neem twig and finds it bitter, but the babool twig tastes better. This chapter is about the habits that keep our body clean, why exercise is good and how to play safely.'),
 [('Clean habits every day',['Our body needs to be clean and free of disease so that it and our mind can work properly. Good habits keep us healthy and happy.','Every day we should brush our teeth, take a shower, comb our hair, wash our hands with soap and keep our nails trimmed and clean.','We should brush our teeth twice a day, once after waking up and once before going to bed, and rinse our mouth every time after eating.','We should wash our hands with soap after using the toilet and after coming home from outside.','A good daily routine includes drinking 6 to 8 glasses of water, eating food, sleeping at least 8 hours and playing outside.']),
  ('Old ways of cleaning',['Long ago people cleaned their teeth with datun, twigs of plants such as neem, karanj and babool. The twig is chewed to make a brush that removes food stuck between teeth and gives the gums a gentle massage.','The modern idea of brushing teeth came from this Indian tradition.','Hair was washed with natural things such as reetha and shikakai.','We can make an eco-friendly home cleaner from orange or lemon peels soaked in vinegar for two weeks. Routines may differ with where we live and how much water we have.']),
  ('Animals keep clean too',['Monkeys sit and groom each other to remove insects from their bodies, and birds use their beaks to clean their feathers.','Many animals have their own ways of keeping their bodies clean.']),
  ('Exercise and play',['When we run fast in a game we breathe faster and deeper, our cheeks may turn red and we may sweat. This is because exercise makes our heart work harder and better.','Exercise strengthens the heart and lungs, makes muscles and bones strong, and keeps the body flexible.','We can exercise in many ways, such as walking like a duck, jumping like a frog, running like a cat or skipping with a rope.','Harpreet\'s grandmother cannot walk much because of the pain in her knees, but she keeps her mind active by playing chess. Both mind and body should be active.','We can play games both outdoors and indoors, such as football, kabaddi, chess and carrom.']),
  ('Playing safely',['A park and a school ground are safe places to play. A busy road, a roof without railings and a construction site are not safe.','In public places there may be strangers. We should not talk to strangers or go with them unless we are with our parents or a trusted adult.','If someone makes us feel uncomfortable, we should tell a trusted adult.'])],
 [('Why should we brush our teeth twice a day?',[('Food stays between the teeth after eating.','Food particles feed germs.'),('Brushing in the morning and before bed removes it.','The mouth stays clean at night too.'),('This keeps teeth strong and breath fresh.','It prevents tooth decay.')]),
  ('Which of these places is safe to play: a school ground, a busy road or a construction site?',[('A busy road has vehicles.','We could be hit.'),('A construction site has machines and sharp things.','We could be hurt.'),('A school ground is safe and open.','It is a safe place to play.')])],
 ('Tell the habits you follow to stay clean and healthy.',['Brush twice a day','Wash hands with soap','Bathe and keep nails short','Drink water and sleep well'],['Washing hands is only needed once a week','Only people who are ill need to exercise']),
 ['Brush teeth twice a day and wash hands with soap.','Drink 6 to 8 glasses of water and sleep 8 hours.','Datun is a traditional way to clean teeth with twigs.','Exercise strengthens the heart, muscles and bones.','Play in safe places and do not go with strangers.'],
 [M('1',1,'How often should we brush our teeth?','Twice a day',[('Once a week','That is too little'),('Never','Brushing keeps teeth healthy')],'Morning and night.'),
  M('2',1,'When should we wash our hands with soap?','After using the toilet and after coming from outdoors',[('Only on Sundays','We wash often'),('Never','Washing removes germs')],'It removes germs.'),
  M('3',1,'What did Moyna\'s Dadu use to clean his teeth?','A neem or babool twig',[('A toothbrush','He used twigs'),('A comb','A comb is for hair')],'This is called datun.'),
  M('4',1,'How many hours should we sleep?','At least 8',[('2','That is too little'),('3','That is too little')],'Sleep helps us grow and stay healthy.'),
  M('5',2,'How many glasses of water should we drink in a day?','6 to 8',[('1','Too few'),('20','Too many')],'Water keeps us healthy.'),
  M('6',2,'What does exercise do to the heart?','Makes it work harder and better',[('Stops it','It makes it stronger'),('Nothing','It makes it stronger')],'Exercise is good for the heart.'),
  M('7',2,'Which is a safe place to play?','A school ground',[('A busy road','Vehicles are dangerous'),('A construction site','Machines are dangerous')],'Open school grounds are safe.'),
  F('8',2,'We can talk to strangers and go with them in a public place.',False,'We should not go with strangers.'),
  F('9',2,'Animals also keep themselves clean.',True,'Monkeys groom and birds clean their feathers.'),
  M('10',2,'Which natural thing was used to wash hair?','Reetha or shikakai',[('Salt','Salt is not for hair'),('Vinegar only','Reetha and shikakai were used')],'These are plant products.'),
  S('11',3,'What do we call the old method of cleaning teeth with twigs?',['datun','Datun'],'Datun came before toothbrushes.'),
  M('12',3,'Why should both mind and body be active?','To stay healthy and happy',[('To make noise','Activity keeps us well'),('To be tired','Activity gives energy')],'Active mind and body keep us well.')],
 keep=['datun','exercise','hygiene'])
